  "presentation_summary": [
    "A previously healthy 11-year-old boy presented with sudden dyspnea, dysphonia, cough, fever, hypoxemia, and inspiratory stridor at rest.",
    "Exam showed barking cough, global chest retractions, no wheeze, and inability to speak beyond short sentences.",
    "Initial data showed temperature 38.3 C, respiratory rate 47/min, SpO2 83% on room air, pH 7.32, and pCO2 47.4 mmHg.",
    "Neck radiograph showed severe glottic/subglottic narrowing with a steeple sign; lateral neck radiograph did not support epiglottitis and chest radiograph was normal.",
    "Respiratory viral panel was otherwise negative, SARS-CoV-2 PCR was positive, blood cultures were negative, and he required PICU monitoring with supplemental oxygen."
  ],
  "snapshot_day": 0,
  "time_anchor": "ed_presentation_after_radiographic_airway_assessment",
  "rankable_evidence_window": "Use presentation symptoms, initial vitals, blood gas, airway radiographs, SARS-CoV-2 PCR, negative blood culture, and early oxygen requirement. The paper's final croup label, PICU disposition, repeated adrenaline/steroid treatment response, transfer to ward, and discharge are record-only.",
  "source_summary": "PMC case report of severe SARS-CoV-2-associated croup with barking cough, dysphonia, stridor at rest, severe hypoxemia, hypercapnic respiratory acidosis, steeple sign, negative bacterial culture, and PICU-level monitoring.",
